  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\n\nShowers will be ongoing early Friday morning as continued lift from \nthe wave and H8 warm advection persist. By the time showers exit \nFriday afternoon, total QPF beginning from Wednesday will range\nfrom around 0.25 to 0.75 inches generally north of a line from \nColumbus to Glenwood to Red Oak, IA. South of these areas, \nexpect totals of 1 to 1.5 inches, and a few spots in our far \nsouthern areas near Beatrice and Fairbury could reach close to 2\ninches.\n\nFriday will also be the start to another warming trend which\nlasts into early next week. 1000-500 mb thicknesses are progged\nto expand over much of the central CONUS as the main H5 ridge \ninches eastward and amplifies. Highs for the weekend climb to \nthe upper 90s to low 100s, cooling slightly to the 90s by Monday\nand Tuesday. Heat Advisory criteria may be met on Sunday over\nmuch of the area with guidance showing indices of 105 to 110 for\na large portion of the forecast area. A few waves may ride the \nmain periphery of the ridge and generate some scattered showers \nand storms after Sunday, but chances remain low (<20%) at this \ntime.",
